At long last, my second ascension.  I've always enjoyed playing monks,
just for the instrinsics.  I always try to play them armourless,
weaponless, and vegetarian.  Typically, I lost vegetarian conduct
after the first floating eye, but this time I opted not to go that
route.  Maybe that's why this one ascended.

The early game was pretty easy, as it usually is for monks.  Early on,
I found both a ring of protection +4 and a blessed +4 orcish helm,
which served me quite well.  I think all that extra AC is what got me
through the early middle game where my monks typically die.

Next big break was finding a wand of wishing in or right below
sokoban.  I wished for the requisite scrolls of charging, boots of
speed, and gaunts of power.   Also wished for the Eye Of Aethiopica
and the final wish was for a ring of slow digestion which would keep
me in good shape the rest of the game.

Things mostly went as planned after that.  Went down and finished both
the castle and Medusa before coming back to finish the quest.  Don't
remember the wishes here, amulet of reflection and helm of brilliance
for sure, and probably a couple magic markers.  Quest wasn't too bad,
Kaen never give me any real trouble, although he did take a bit to
finish off.

I discovered Fort Lud, and used the proceeds of that trip to get the
elusive naked ac 0 (I had ac 1 before that).  Enchanted up my robe,
helm, gaunts and boots to nice mix of +4/+5 with the help of my magic
markers.

I also geno'd L ; h and cockatrices and disenchanters.  The latter two
came from thrones, and the former came from blessed scrolls I had
written or found.  I would later find another scroll and use it on T,
just because they were irritating (I just like things to stay dead,
what can I say).

Gehennom proceeded fairly uneventfully.  Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Orcus,
and Jubilex all went down without too much trouble.  Vlad's still a
massive wimp.  About half way down, I spent a bit of time alchemizing
some extra healing potions and got up to 340 hp (which I was gonna
need later).

Finding the Vibrating Square took quite a bit of effort, and one of
the minor demons summoned Yeenoghu, who I managed to lose track of for
a bit when he escaped upstairs.  I was fairly worried that he'd summon
Demogorgon, but luckily I managed to get him before that happened.

After the square was found, I made a quick run up to orcus town, to
make use of the altar there for b/u/c purposes.  In retrospect, I
could have used the one in the sanctum.  I made the run up to the
wizard, used a wand of death, and the race was on.

Slugging my way through to the sanctum wasn't too bad.  Got lucky and
intrinsic searching found the secret door on one of the first squares
I moved past.  High priest gave me a bit of trouble, down to 130 or so
hp, of my 340, although I was probably down 100 or so before I started
fighting him.

Got the amulet, and started the run up.  Mysterious force made seldom
few appearances, which was nice.  A straight run up was over pretty
quick, with one scary moment in the valley.  A green slime happened to
be on the automove path and managed to hit me as I ran by.  I luckily
had enough time to pull out a wand of fire and fix that problem. 
Picked up a few gems I had stashed on dlvl 1, and then entered the
plane of earth.

The wizard made two appearances on earth, both times going down
quickly to my wand of death.  None of the planes gave me any real
trouble, although I did have to rest up in a steam vortex after I
rough fight with an air elemental.

The astral plane gave me a lot of trouble.  I started on the left,
went to the center, where death was, although he had leaked out and
was on the east side of the door behind a few ants, so I thought I'd
be ok.  Later, as the room was getting empty, he came after me.  It
was seriously rough going, with nowhere to run, and he drained 200 of
my 340 max hp away.  I finally took him down on the run to the left. 
Twas there that I quaffed my first and only remaining potion of gain
level (others had been alchemized), and reached lvl 16, to restore a
bit of the hp loss.

The left was the wrong one, and famine got in the way going in and
coming out.  Managed to circle around the revived death and only lost
a couple more max hp before running back up into the middle to learn
that it was the wrong one as well.  On the way to the right, I pulled
out a wand of teleport and started clearing paths.  Had to kill famine
again, but avoided death.

The right was finally the correct way, and with the wands of teleport
and death,
made it past pestilence and through all the angels and priests to the
altar.  Managed to anger the high priest with a badly aimed teleport,
but still survived long enough to offer the amulet and ascend.

